    [
     1,
     "\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<div dir=\"ltr\">\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Calibri,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0);background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">\r\nTsakala</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Calibri,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0);background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">\r\n<br>\r\n</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Calibri,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0);background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">\r\nThere are demonstrations of creating designs for study areas with multiple strata in Chapter 3 of the Distance for Windows Users Guide.  It is example 4, that provides step-by-step instructions, the first page of which looks like this</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Calibri,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0);background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">\r\n<br>\r\n</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Calibri,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0);background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">\r\n<img style=\"max-width:100%\" size=\"115189\" src=\"https://groups.google.com/group/distance-sampling/attach/113d6fb364c0d/image.png?part=0.1&amp;view=1\"></div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Calibri,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0);background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">\r\n<br>\r\n</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Calibri,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0);background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">\r\nFollowing those instructions and importing the shape files provided with Distance for Windows in the Sample Projects folder (as described in the Users Guide), you can produce a shape file with four strata (from northern Mexico) in your Distance for Windows\r\n window, looking something like this:</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Calibri,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0);background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">\r\n<br>\r\n</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Calibri,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0);background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">\r\n<img style=\"max-width:100%\" size=\"32513\" src=\"https://groups.google.com/group/distance-sampling/attach/113d6fb364c0d/image.png?part=0.2&amp;view=1\"></div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Calibri,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0);background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">\r\nI have highlighted the strata boundaries as they are a bit difficult to see against the blue background.</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Calibri,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0);background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">\r\n<br>\r\n</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Calibri,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0);background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">\r\nAn exercise similar to this, based around this Mexico study area is presented (and narrated) in our online workshop materials, Chapter 4. Link below.<br>\r\n</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Calibri,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0);background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">\r\n<br>\r\n</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Calibri,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0);background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">\r\n<a href=\"https://workshops.distancesampling.org/online-course/syllabus/Chapter4/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://workshops.distancesampling.org/online-course/syllabus/Chapter4/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792472308166000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2tVeW9r4GL4nI3bvUUz_I9\">https://workshops.distancesampling.org/online-course/syllabus/Chapter4/</a><br>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div style=\"width:100%;margin-top:16px;margin-bottom:16px;max-width:800px;min-width:424px\">\r\n<table role=\"presentation\" style=\"padding:12px 36px 12px 12px;width:100%;border-width:1px;border-style:solid;border-color:rgb(200,200,200);border-radius:2px\">\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr style=\"border-spacing:0px\" valign=\"top\">\r\n<td style=\"width:100%\">\r\n<div style=\"font-size:21px;font-weight:300;margin-right:8px;font-family:&quot;wf_segoe-ui_light&quot;,&quot;Segoe UI Light&quot;,&quot;Segoe WP Light&quot;,&quot;Segoe UI&quot;,&quot;Segoe WP&quot;,Tahoma,Arial,sans-serif;margin-bottom:12px\">\r\n<a href=\"https://workshops.distancesampling.org/online-course/syllabus/Chapter4/\" style=\"text-decoration:none;color:var(--themePrimary)\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://workshops.distancesampling.org/online-course/syllabus/Chapter4/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792472308166000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2tVeW9r4GL4nI3bvUUz_I9\">Chapter 4 Survey design and field methods</a></div>\r\n<div style=\"font-size:14px;max-height:100px;color:rgb(102,102,102);font-family:&quot;wf_segoe-ui_normal&quot;,&quot;Segoe UI&quot;,&quot;Segoe WP&quot;,Tahoma,Arial,sans-serif;margin-bottom:12px;margin-right:8px;overflow:hidden\">\r\nTeaching distance sampling through video lectures and computer exercises.</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-size:14px;font-weight:400;color:rgb(166,166,166);font-family:&quot;wf_segoe-ui_normal&quot;,&quot;Segoe UI&quot;,&quot;Segoe WP&quot;,Tahoma,Arial,sans-serif\">\r\n<a href=\"http://workshops.distancesampling.org\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://workshops.distancesampling.org&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792472308166000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1cjnqPCr6lnmHEnO3A8-jw\">workshops.distancesampling.org</a></div>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Calibri,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0);background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">\r\nIf you work carefully through those exercises (Users Guide and online workshop) you will gain experience in designing multi-strata surveys such as the one you intend to perform. The difference will be that you will be importing the shape files relevant to your\r\n study area, rather than the Mexico shapefiles.<br>\r\n</div>\r\n<div></div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Calibri,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\n<br>\r\n</div>\r\n<hr style=\"display:inline-block;width:98%\">\r\n<div dir=\"ltr\"><font style=\"font-size:11pt\" face=\"Calibri, sans-serif\" color=\"#000000\"><b>From:</b> Papy Tsakala &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">tsakal...@gmail.com</a>&gt;<br>\r\n<b>Sent:</b> 04 March 2023 20:59<br>\r\n<b>To:</b> Eric Rexstad &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">Eric.R...@st-andrews.ac.uk</a>&gt;<br>\r\n<b>Cc:</b> distance-sampling &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">distance...@googlegroups.com</a>&gt;<br>\r\n<b>Subject:</b> Re: [distance-sampling] Request</font>\r\n<div> </div>\r\n</div></div>"
    ],
