     3,
     "<br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><div dir=\"ltr\" class=\"gmail_attr\">Le dim. 5 mars 2023 à 15:56, Eric Rexstad &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">Eric.R...@st-andrews.ac.uk</a>&gt; a écrit :<br></div><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\">\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<div dir=\"ltr\">\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Calibri,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0);background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">\r\nTsakala</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Calibri,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0);background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">\r\n<br>\r\n</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Calibri,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0);background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">\r\nThere are demonstrations of creating designs for study areas with multiple strata in Chapter 3 of the Distance for Windows Users Guide.  It is example 4, that provides step-by-step instructions, the first page of which looks like this</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Calibri,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0);background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">\r\n<br>\r\n</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Calibri,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0);background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">\r\n<img style=\"max-width:100%\" size=\"115189\"></div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Calibri,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0);background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">\r\n<br>\r\n</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Calibri,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0);background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">\r\nFollowing those instructions and importing the shape files provided with Distance for Windows in the Sample Projects folder (as described in the Users Guide), you can produce a shape file with four strata (from northern Mexico) in your Distance for Windows\r\n window, looking something like this:</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Calibri,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0);background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">\r\n<br>\r\n</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Calibri,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0);background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">\r\n<img style=\"max-width:100%\" size=\"32513\"></div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Calibri,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0);background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">\r\nI have highlighted the strata boundaries as they are a bit difficult to see against the blue background.</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Calibri,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0);background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">\r\n<br>\r\n</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Calibri,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0);background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">\r\nAn exercise similar to this, based around this Mexico study area is presented (and narrated) in our online workshop materials, Chapter 4. Link below.<br>\r\n</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Calibri,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0);background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">\r\n<br>\r\n</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Calibri,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0);background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">\r\n<a href=\"https://workshops.distancesampling.org/online-course/syllabus/Chapter4/\" rel=\"noreferrer nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://workshops.distancesampling.org/online-course/syllabus/Chapter4/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792472308171000&amp;usg=AOvVaw32U1W-KHRVCttRtOz0QOHj\">https://workshops.distancesampling.org/online-course/syllabus/Chapter4/</a><br>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div style=\"width:100%;margin-top:16px;margin-bottom:16px;max-width:800px;min-width:424px\">\r\n<table role=\"presentation\" style=\"padding:12px 36px 12px 12px;width:100%;border-width:1px;border-style:solid;border-color:rgb(200,200,200);border-radius:2px\">\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr style=\"border-spacing:0px\" valign=\"top\">\r\n<td style=\"width:100%\">\r\n<div style=\"font-size:21px;font-weight:300;margin-right:8px;font-family:&quot;wf_segoe-ui_light&quot;,&quot;Segoe UI Light&quot;,&quot;Segoe WP Light&quot;,&quot;Segoe UI&quot;,&quot;Segoe WP&quot;,Tahoma,Arial,sans-serif;margin-bottom:12px\">\r\n<a href=\"https://workshops.distancesampling.org/online-course/syllabus/Chapter4/\" style=\"text-decoration:none;color:var(--themePrimary)\" rel=\"noreferrer nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://workshops.distancesampling.org/online-course/syllabus/Chapter4/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792472308171000&amp;usg=AOvVaw32U1W-KHRVCttRtOz0QOHj\">Chapter 4 Survey design and field methods</a></div>\r\n<div style=\"font-size:14px;max-height:100px;color:rgb(102,102,102);font-family:&quot;wf_segoe-ui_normal&quot;,&quot;Segoe UI&quot;,&quot;Segoe WP&quot;,Tahoma,Arial,sans-serif;margin-bottom:12px;margin-right:8px;overflow:hidden\">\r\nTeaching distance sampling through video lectures and computer exercises.</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-size:14px;font-weight:400;color:rgb(166,166,166);font-family:&quot;wf_segoe-ui_normal&quot;,&quot;Segoe UI&quot;,&quot;Segoe WP&quot;,Tahoma,Arial,sans-serif\">\r\n<a href=\"http://workshops.distancesampling.org\" rel=\"noreferrer nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://workshops.distancesampling.org&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792472308171000&amp;usg=AOvVaw15L4KKU0dQhA3LEgq_XPXO\">workshops.distancesampling.org</a></div>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Calibri,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0);background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">\r\nIf you work carefully through those exercises (Users Guide and online workshop) you will gain experience in designing multi-strata surveys such as the one you intend to perform. The difference will be that you will be importing the shape files relevant to your\r\n study area, rather than the Mexico shapefiles.<br>\r\n</div>\r\n<div></div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Calibri,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\n<br>\r\n</div>\r\n<hr style=\"display:inline-block;width:98%\">\r\n<div dir=\"ltr\"><font style=\"font-size:11pt\" face=\"Calibri, sans-serif\" color=\"#000000\"><b>From:</b> Papy Tsakala &lt;<a href rel=\"noreferrer nofollow\" data-email-masked>tsakal...@gmail.com</a>&gt;<br>\r\n<b>Sent:</b> 04 March 2023 20:59<br>\r\n<b>To:</b> Eric Rexstad &lt;<a href rel=\"noreferrer nofollow\" data-email-masked>Eric.R...@st-andrews.ac.uk</a>&gt;<br>\r\n<b>Cc:</b> distance-sampling &lt;<a href rel=\"noreferrer nofollow\" data-email-masked>distance...@googlegroups.com</a>&gt;<br>\r\n<b>Subject:</b> Re: [distance-sampling] Request</font>\r\n<div> </div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">Thanks for your help,\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">For being more accurate and precise, I am using Distance 7.4 for Microsoft </div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">I am able to design for a study area with one strata, but my study area is stratified in 7 stratum.It&#39;s a REDD+ Concession; but we&#39;ll focus our surveys on 4stratum.</div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">A tutorial of more than one strata will be helpfull for us.</div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">Regards,</div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">Tsakala </div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\"><br>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<br>\r\n<div>\r\n<div dir=\"ltr\">Le sam. 4 mars 2023 à 12:05, Eric Rexstad &lt;<a href rel=\"noreferrer nofollow\" data-email-masked>Eric.R...@st-andrews.ac.uk</a>&gt; a écrit :<br>\r\n</div>\r\n<blockquote style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\">\r\n<div dir=\"ltr\">\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Calibri,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0);background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">\r\nTsakalambutu</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Calibri,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0);background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">\r\n<br>\r\n</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Calibri,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0);background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">\r\nWe have a tutorial for a multiple stratum survey using the R package <code>dssd</code>​ you can follow at this link:</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Calibri,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0);background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">\r\n<br>\r\n</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Calibri,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0);background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">\r\n<a href=\"http://examples.distancesampling.org/dssd-multi-strata/MultiStrataVignette-distill.html\" rel=\"noreferrer nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://examples.distancesampling.org/dssd-multi-strata/MultiStrataVignette-distill.html&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792472308171000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2BDgaQ2FO4ap_FWxEa8FE3\">http://examples.distancesampling.org/dssd-multi-strata/MultiStrataVignette-distill.html</a><br>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div style=\"width:100%;margin-top:16px;margin-bottom:16px;max-width:800px;min-width:424px\">\r\n<table role=\"presentation\" style=\"padding:12px 36px 12px 12px;width:100%;border-width:1px;border-style:solid;border-color:rgb(200,200,200);border-radius:2px\">\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr style=\"border-spacing:0px\" valign=\"top\">\r\n<td style=\"width:100%\">\r\n<div style=\"font-size:21px;font-weight:300;margin-right:8px;font-family:&quot;wf_segoe-ui_light&quot;,&quot;Segoe UI Light&quot;,&quot;Segoe WP Light&quot;,&quot;Segoe UI&quot;,&quot;Segoe WP&quot;,Tahoma,Arial,sans-serif;margin-bottom:12px\">\r\n<a href=\"http://examples.distancesampling.org/dssd-multi-strata/MultiStrataVignette-distill.html\" style=\"text-decoration:none\" rel=\"noreferrer nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://examples.distancesampling.org/dssd-multi-strata/MultiStrataVignette-distill.html&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792472308171000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2BDgaQ2FO4ap_FWxEa8FE3\">Multiple Strata in dssd</a></div>\r\n<div style=\"font-size:14px;max-height:100px;color:rgb(102,102,102);font-family:&quot;wf_segoe-ui_normal&quot;,&quot;Segoe UI&quot;,&quot;Segoe WP&quot;,Tahoma,Arial,sans-serif;margin-bottom:12px;margin-right:8px;overflow:hidden\">\r\nDesigning distance sampling surveys containing more than one stratum.</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-size:14px;font-weight:400;color:rgb(166,166,166);font-family:&quot;wf_segoe-ui_normal&quot;,&quot;Segoe UI&quot;,&quot;Segoe WP&quot;,Tahoma,Arial,sans-serif\">\r\n<a href=\"http://examples.distancesampling.org\" rel=\"noreferrer nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://examples.distancesampling.org&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792472308171000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3BY_n-EBAXnziMFi6BcXpO\">examples.distancesampling.org</a></div>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Calibri,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0);background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">\r\nIf you wish to use Distance for Windows, there are examples for both single and two strata. They can be found in Chapter 3, Getting Started of the Distance Users Guide.</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Calibri,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0);background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">\r\n<br>\r\n</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Calibri,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0);background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">\r\nIf you need more assistance after consulting these, please get back in touch.<br>\r\n</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Calibri,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0);background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">\r\n<br>\r\n</div>\r\n<div></div>\r\n<hr style=\"display:inline-block;width:98%\">\r\n<div dir=\"ltr\"><font style=\"font-size:11pt\" face=\"Calibri, sans-serif\" color=\"#000000\"><b>From:</b>\r\n<a href rel=\"noreferrer nofollow\" data-email-masked>\r\ndistance...@googlegroups.com</a> &lt;<a href rel=\"noreferrer nofollow\" data-email-masked>distance...@googlegroups.com</a>&gt; on behalf of\r\n<a href rel=\"noreferrer nofollow\" data-email-masked>\r\ntsakal...@gmail.com</a> &lt;<a href rel=\"noreferrer nofollow\" data-email-masked>tsakal...@gmail.com</a>&gt;<br>\r\n<b>Sent:</b> 04 March 2023 10:41<br>\r\n<b>To:</b> distance-sampling &lt;<a href rel=\"noreferrer nofollow\" data-email-masked>distance...@googlegroups.com</a>&gt;<br>\r\n<b>Subject:</b> [distance-sampling] Request</font>\r\n<div> </div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>Hi everyone;\r\n<div>I would like to get a help about designing a sampling plan of a study area stratified in 5 strata. In fact; I want to make transects of one kilometer randomly and systematically for ecological survey.</div>\r\n<div>Is there any one who can help with a tutorial?</div>\r\n<div><br>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>Kind regards</div>\r\n<p></p>\r\n-- <br>\r\nYou received this message because you are subscribed to the Google Groups &quot;distance-sampling&quot; group.<br>\r\nTo unsubscribe from this group and stop receiving emails from it, send an email to\r\n<a href rel=\"noreferrer nofollow\" data-email-masked>\r\ndistance-sampl...@googlegroups.com</a>.<br>\r\nTo view this discussion on the web visit <a href=\"https://groups.google.com/d/msgid/distance-sampling/c88d6f24-9d80-4092-b289-c8375b3c5612n%40googlegroups.com?utm_medium=email&amp;utm_source=footer\" rel=\"noreferrer nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://groups.google.com/d/msgid/distance-sampling/c88d6f24-9d80-4092-b289-c8375b3c5612n%2540googlegroups.com?utm_medium%3Demail%26utm_source%3Dfooter&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792472308172000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0eP5m0__6261FRZvp6_JAx\">\r\nhttps://groups.google.com/d/msgid/distance-sampling/c88d6f24-9d80-4092-b289-c8375b